# Navigation Migration Phase 3 — INCOMPLETE (corrected 2026-07-26)

> Earlier revisions of this rule claimed "COMPLETED — zero remaining legacy
> patterns" and listed a `SettingsRoute` enum (11 cases). Both claims were
> false when audited on 2026-07-26 (production-readiness audit, MASTER_TODO
> PR-28/PR-41): **no `SettingsRoute` enum exists**, and 15 legacy links remain.

## Remaining legacy patterns (verify with `rg "NavigationLink\(destination:" Fit33/`)

- `Fit33/SettingsView.swift` — **13× `NavigationLink(destination:)`** (one of
  them also uses deprecated `isActive:` for DevMenu).
- `Fit33/ProfileView.swift` — **2× `NavigationLink(destination:)`** plus
  `isActive:` bindings (`showWorkoutHistory`, `showFriendsList`,
  `showReceivedWorkouts`).

Finishing the migration = introduce a `SettingsRoute` enum +
`.navigationDestination(for:)` in SettingsView, and convert ProfileView's
remaining links/bindings. Tracked as MASTER_TODO PR-28.

## What IS done (verified)

- All other surfaces (~14 files) converted to `NavigationLink(value:)` +
  `.navigationDestination(for:)` / `.navigationDestination(isPresented:)`.
- Route enums that exist: `DashboardRoute` (DashboardView.swift),
  `ProfileRoute`, `ProgressRoute`, `PersonalizedProgramRoute`, `DevMenuRoute`,
  `InBodyRoute`, `UnitSettingsRoute`, and the
  `CloudScheduleDayRoute` / `ProgramScheduleDayRoute` /
  `ProgramScheduleWorkoutRoute` / `ProgramScheduleExerciseRoute` structs.
- Hashable conformances added: WorkoutProgram, SmartProgramTemplate,
  SmartActiveProgram, SmartProgramDay, ActiveChallenge, ActiveGroupChallenge,
  CardioWorkoutDTO (all hash by `id`).

## Key Pattern: DashboardView

DashboardView's navigation destinations were extracted into a
`DashboardNavigationDestinations` ViewModifier to prevent Swift type-checker
timeout on the large body.

## Rule for new code

Never add a new `NavigationLink(destination:)` or `isActive:` link — always
use value-based navigation with a route enum + `.navigationDestination(for:)`.
